{
  "episode": 100,
  "source": "assets/video/ep100.mp4",
  "model": "base",
  "duration": 347.76525,
  "segments": [
    {
      "i": 1,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 7.0,
      "text": "Journey to the West, chapter 100, a terrible robbery."
    },
    {
      "i": 2,
      "start": 12.0,
      "end": 17.0,
      "text": "For over a month, the traveler stayed at Squire Koo's house."
    },
    {
      "i": 3,
      "start": 18.0,
      "end": 23.0,
      "text": "Every time they tried to leave the Squire begged them to stay longer."
    },
    {
      "i": 4,
      "start": 24.0,
      "end": 30.0,
      "text": "Finally, one morning during breakfast, the Tang Monk insisted on leaving."
    },
    {
      "i": 5,
      "start": 32.0,
      "end": 35.0,
      "text": "We'll never fetch the true scriptures if we stay here."
    },
    {
      "i": 6,
      "start": 36.0,
      "end": 38.0,
      "text": "Please don't leave."
    },
    {
      "i": 7,
      "start": 38.0,
      "end": 39.0,
      "text": "Said Squire Koo."
    },
    {
      "i": 8,
      "start": 39.0,
      "end": 44.0,
      "text": "You are very important monks. Having you as guests is a good deed."
    },
    {
      "i": 9,
      "start": 45.0,
      "end": 47.0,
      "text": "I'd like to stay here."
    },
    {
      "i": 10,
      "start": 47.0,
      "end": 50.0,
      "text": "Said Bajay. He took a bite of a peach."
    },
    {
      "i": 11,
      "start": 51.0,
      "end": 52.0,
      "text": "No, master's right."
    },
    {
      "i": 12,
      "start": 52.0,
      "end": 53.0,
      "text": "Said Wukong."
    },
    {
      "i": 13,
      "start": 54.0,
      "end": 56.0,
      "text": "We must continue our journey."
    },
    {
      "i": 14,
      "start": 57.0,
      "end": 59.0,
      "text": "Lady Koo grew angry."
    },
    {
      "i": 15,
      "start": 59.0,
      "end": 61.0,
      "text": "You monks are ungrateful."
    },
    {
      "i": 16,
      "start": 62.0,
      "end": 64.0,
      "text": "We have fed you and taken care of you."
    },
    {
      "i": 17,
      "start": 65.0,
      "end": 67.0,
      "text": "Yet you can't wait to leave."
    },
    {
      "i": 18,
      "start": 68.0,
      "end": 69.0,
      "text": "We are very grateful."
    },
    {
      "i": 19,
      "start": 69.0,
      "end": 70.0,
      "text": "Said the Tang Monk."
    },
    {
      "i": 20,
      "start": 71.0,
      "end": 73.0,
      "text": "But we cannot stay any longer."
    },
    {
      "i": 21,
      "start": 75.0,
      "end": 79.0,
      "text": "After breakfast, Wu Jing got the horse from Squire Koo's stable."
    },
    {
      "i": 22,
      "start": 80.0,
      "end": 82.0,
      "text": "Bajay gathered the bags."
    },
    {
      "i": 23,
      "start": 82.0,
      "end": 87.0,
      "text": "The Tang Monk thanked Squire and Lady Koo and the traveler's headed west."
    },
    {
      "i": 24,
      "start": 92.0,
      "end": 93.0,
      "text": "They are ungrateful."
    },
    {
      "i": 25,
      "start": 93.0,
      "end": 95.0,
      "text": "Muttered Lady Koo."
    },
    {
      "i": 26,
      "start": 99.0,
      "end": 103.0,
      "text": "The next morning, Lady Koo ran into the town's courthouse."
    },
    {
      "i": 27,
      "start": 104.0,
      "end": 106.0,
      "text": "Tears filled her eyes."
    },
    {
      "i": 28,
      "start": 107.0,
      "end": 109.0,
      "text": "I must speak with the judge."
    },
    {
      "i": 29,
      "start": 109.0,
      "end": 110.0,
      "text": "She cried."
    },
    {
      "i": 30,
      "start": 111.0,
      "end": 113.0,
      "text": "The judge rushed to her."
    },
    {
      "i": 31,
      "start": 114.0,
      "end": 116.0,
      "text": "Lady Koo. What's wrong?"
    },
    {
      "i": 32,
      "start": 116.0,
      "end": 119.0,
      "text": "Robbers broke into her house last night."
    },
    {
      "i": 33,
      "start": 119.0,
      "end": 121.0,
      "text": "Said Lady Koo breathlessly."
    },
    {
      "i": 34,
      "start": 122.0,
      "end": 126.0,
      "text": "They stole many valuable items and two of our horses."
    },
    {
      "i": 35,
      "start": 127.0,
      "end": 129.0,
      "text": "Squire Koo tried to stop them."
    },
    {
      "i": 36,
      "start": 129.0,
      "end": 130.0,
      "text": "But the robbers."
    },
    {
      "i": 37,
      "start": 131.0,
      "end": 134.0,
      "text": "They killed my husband."
    },
    {
      "i": 38,
      "start": 137.0,
      "end": 139.0,
      "text": "Lady Koo burst into tears."
    },
    {
      "i": 39,
      "start": 139.0,
      "end": 141.0,
      "text": "The judge gasped."
    },
    {
      "i": 40,
      "start": 141.0,
      "end": 144.0,
      "text": "Oh no. Did you see the robbers?"
    },
    {
      "i": 41,
      "start": 145.0,
      "end": 147.0,
      "text": "Lady Koo sniffed."
    },
    {
      "i": 42,
      "start": 147.0,
      "end": 148.0,
      "text": "Yes."
    },
    {
      "i": 43,
      "start": 148.0,
      "end": 150.0,
      "text": "And I know who they are."
    }
  ]
}
